title: 'a-clock: remove wake-from-sleep feature entirely (it blocked alarms)'
summary: Removed the macOS wake-from-sleep feature completely because its osascript 'with administrator privileges' pmset call prompted at alarm-fire time and the modal blocked the alarm from actually triggering the file — unacceptable for an alarm clock. Deleted src/lib/wake.ts and the schedule_wake/cancel_wake/run_osascript Rust commands, removed the wake effect + fireTick + the Wake Mac toggle and the wakeFromSleep setting, and moved the still-needed nextOccurrence helper into mobileAlarms.ts. No osascript/pmset remains anywhere. Rebuilt and reinstalled; alarms now fire unblocked.
symbols_touched:
  - '#tauri-core'
  - '#mobile-alarms'
  - '#alarms-view'
  - '#storage'
files_modified:
  - src/App.tsx
  - src/components/AlarmsView.tsx
  - src/types.ts
  - src/lib/storage.ts
  - src/lib/mobileAlarms.ts
  - src-tauri/src/lib.rs
decisions:
  - id: remove-wake-feature
    decision: Remove wake-from-sleep entirely rather than keep patching it
    rationale: The admin prompt fired at alarm-fire time and blocked the alarm from triggering its file — it broke the app's core function. No amount of dedup fixes a feature that requires a root prompt; removing it guarantees alarms are never blocked.
learnings:
  - A feature that requires a root/admin prompt (pmset via osascript) can block the app's primary function when the modal appears at the wrong time; for a foreground alarm, never gate firing behind a privileged prompt.
  - 'The reliable cross-platform alarm approach is: JS scheduler while the app runs (kept alive by the tray + KeepAlive agent) on desktop, OS-scheduled notifications on mobile, and local audio/video files for in-overlay playback.'
